---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Spectrum from '../components/Spectrum.astro';
import Term from '../components/Term.astro';
import instruments from '../data/instruments.json';
const ROLE = { Navigate: ['Transitional', 'tag-mode1'], Reshape: ['Structural', 'tag-mode2'], Either: ['Either', 'tag-hybrid'] };
const LEVER = {
  process: ['Process improvement', 'chip-cost'], scale: ['Scale and learning', 'chip-cost'], capital: ['Capital cost', 'chip-cost'],
  competition: ['Competition', 'chip-margin'], disintermediation: ['Disintermediation', 'chip-margin'], risk: ['Risk transfer', 'chip-margin'],
  transfer: ['Financial transfer', 'chip-transfer'], innovation: ['Innovation incentive', 'chip-innovation'], payment: ['Payment design', 'chip-structural'],
  correction: ['Price correction', 'chip-structural'], voluntary: ['Voluntary payer', 'chip-structural'],
};
const sorted = [...instruments].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
---
<Page
  title="Instruments"
  description="The anatomy of a financial instrument, and a focused catalogue of market and financial instruments described by role, levers fired, kind of money and when each holds after exit."
  lede="Every instrument is a set of answers to the same few questions. The catalogue that follows is focused rather than comprehensive: each entry says what matters for cost-effectiveness."
  bands={true}
>
  <section id="anatomy" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white scroll-mt-28">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">The Anatomy of an Instrument</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-10">Every financial instrument, from simple grants to complex impact bonds, is built from the same components. Three questions define any intervention; knowing the answers lets you see through jargon to what an instrument actually does.</p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 mb-1">1. If it fails, who pays?</div><div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-2">Risk allocation</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Who absorbs the loss if the investment doesn't work? At one extreme, the investor. At the other, a donor or government covers the loss, which is a guarantee. Guarantees shift risk from those who won't bear it to those who can.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 mb-1">2. How subsidized is the money?</div><div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-2">Return expectations</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Commercial capital wants market-rate returns; grants expect none; <Term>concessional capital</Term> sits in between. Concessional capital is scarce, which is why staying as commercial as possible matters.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 mb-1">3. Pay for effort or results?</div><div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-2">Payment trigger</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Traditional funding pays when you act; <Term t="Results-Based Financing (RBF)">outcome-based funding</Term> pays only when results are verified. Outcome-linking creates accountability, but only works when outcomes are measurable and verification is affordable.</p></div>
      </div>
      <Spectrum label="1. If it fails, who pays?" question="Who absorbs the loss if things go wrong?" left="Investor or borrower" right="Donor or taxpayer" gradient="bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-300 to-blue-600" points={[{pos:10,label:'Commercial loan'},{pos:50,label:'Guarantee'},{pos:90,label:'Grant'}]} />
      <Spectrum label="2. How subsidized is the money?" question="What return does the capital expect?" left="Full market return" right="Free (grant)" gradient="bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-700 to-emerald-400" points={[{pos:10,label:'Equity'},{pos:38,label:'Commercial debt'},{pos:68,label:'Concessional'},{pos:92,label:'Grant'}]} />
      <Spectrum label="3. Pay for effort or results?" question="When does money flow?" left="Pay when they act" right="Pay when we see results" gradient="bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-400 to-amber-500" points={[{pos:10,label:'Grant or loan'},{pos:50,label:'Milestone-based'},{pos:90,label:'Impact bond'}]} />
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-4">
        <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">More risk transfer</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Necessary when the market genuinely can't bear the risk, but it costs the funder more and may weaken market discipline. Absorb only what's necessary.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">More subsidy</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Necessary when deals can't close at commercial rates. Concessional capital is scarce: using less stretches it further.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200"><div class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">More outcome-linkage</div><p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Better accountability and incentives, but verification costs money and not everything is measurable.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-xl p-6 mt-8">
        <div class="font-serif text-xl text-slate-900 mb-2">The Fourth Dimension: Verification</div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <div><div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Verification is feasible when</div><ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1"><li>Outcomes are clearly defined and measurable</li><li>Attribution is possible</li><li>Verification costs are proportionate to deal size</li><li>Timeframes allow outcomes to be observed</li></ul></div>
          <div><div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Verification is difficult when</div><ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1"><li>Outcomes take years to materialize</li><li>Many factors affect results</li><li>Measurement is expensive relative to the intervention</li><li>Gaming or manipulation risks distort behavior</li></ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mt-8">The anatomy describes what the funder gives up. Whether that buys durable impact depends on two further things: the <a class="text-blue-800 underline" href="/framework/mechanisms/">lever</a> the instrument fires, and whether the money is contingent or a flow that must continue. The catalogue below records both.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="catalogue" class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50 scroll-mt-28">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">Instrument Catalogue</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8">{instruments.length} instruments, each described by the lever it fires or the payer it creates. For broader catalogues of instrument mechanics, see <a class="text-blue-800 underline" href="/related-work/">related work</a>.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-3 mb-4 no-print" id="filters" hidden>
        <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search instruments" aria-label="Search instruments" class="flex-1 border border-slate-300 rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white" />
        <select id="role" aria-label="Filter by role" class="border border-slate-300 rounded-lg px-3 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white">
          <option value="">All roles</option><option value="Navigate">Transitional</option><option value="Reshape">Structural</option><option value="Either">Either</option>
        </select>
        <select id="lever" aria-label="Filter by lever" class="border border-slate-300 rounded-lg px-3 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white">
          <option value="">All levers</option>
          <optgroup label="Cost reduction"><option value="process">Process improvement</option><option value="scale">Scale and learning</option><option value="capital">Capital cost</option></optgroup>
          <optgroup label="Margin reduction"><option value="competition">Competition</option><option value="disintermediation">Disintermediation</option><option value="risk">Risk transfer</option></optgroup>
          <optgroup label="Parallel approaches"><option value="transfer">Financial transfer</option><option value="innovation">Innovation incentive</option><option value="payment">Payment design</option><option value="correction">Price correction</option><option value="voluntary">Voluntary payer</option></optgroup>
        </select>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-6" id="count" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4" id="grid">
        {sorted.map((i) => (
          <details class="instrument bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5 card-hover" id={i.id} data-role={i.role} data-levers={i.leverKeys.join(' ')} data-text={`${i.name} ${i.use}`.toLowerCase()}>
            <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
              <span class={`tag ${ROLE[i.role][1]}`}>{ROLE[i.role][0]}</span>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-3 mb-2 font-sans text-base">{i.name}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">{i.use}</p>
              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1">{i.leverKeys.map((k) => <span class={`chip ${LEVER[k][1]}`}>{LEVER[k][0]}</span>)}</div>
              <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-blue-900 mt-3">Details</span>
            </summary>
            <dl class="mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 text-sm grid gap-2">
              <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Money</dt><dd class="text-slate-600">{i.money}</dd></div>
              <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Holds after exit if</dt><dd class="text-slate-600">{i.holds}</dd></div>
              {i.example && <div><dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Example</dt><dd class="text-slate-600">{i.exampleLink ? <a class="text-blue-800 underline" href={i.exampleLink}>{i.example}</a> : i.example}</dd></div>}
              <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mt-1">
                <div><dt class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Strengths</dt><dd><ul class="text-slate-600 space-y-1">{i.strengths.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-700 uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Limitations</dt><dd><ul class="text-slate-600 space-y-1">{i.limitations.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul></dd></div>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-amber-50 p-3 rounded mt-1"><dt class="font-semibold text-amber-900 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Watch for</dt><dd class="text-slate-700">{i.watch}</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var f = document.getElementById('filters'); f.hidden = false;
      var q = document.getElementById('q'), role = document.getElementById('role'), lever = document.getElementById('lever');
      var cards = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('#grid .instrument')), count = document.getElementById('count');
      function apply() {
        var t = q.value.trim().toLowerCase(), r = role.value, l = lever.value, n = 0;
        cards.forEach(function (c) {
          var ok = (!t || c.dataset.text.indexOf(t) > -1) && (!r || c.dataset.role === r) && (!l || (' ' + c.dataset.levers + ' ').indexOf(' ' + l + ' ') > -1);
          c.style.display = ok ? '' : 'none'; if (ok) n++;
        });
        count.textContent = 'Showing ' + n + ' of ' + cards.length + ' instruments';
      }
      [q, role, lever].forEach(function (el) { el.addEventListener('input', apply); });
      if (location.hash) { var el = document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1)); if (el && el.tagName === 'DETAILS') el.open = true; }
      apply();
    })();
  </script>
</Page>
